wr/preview/mmwrhtml/figures/m727a2t.gif","alt":"TABLE. Number of emergency department visits for selected respiratory disease indicators — six hospitals, San Diego, California,\nSeptember 24–October 26, 2007\nPre-fire period* Fire period† Excess no. of\nDisease indicator No. of visits Mean per day No. of visits Mean per day visits per day§ p-value¶\nChief complaint**\nRespiratory syndrome†† 2,681 134.1 816 163.2 29.2 <0.001\nAsthma 136 6.8 96 19.2 12.4 <0.001\nBronchitis 8 0.4 4 0.8 0.4 0.2\nChest pain 1,240 62.0 302 60.4 -1.6 0.4\nCough 314 15.7 73 14.6 -1.1 0.5\nDyspnea 971 48.6 363 72.6 24.1 <0.001\nDiagnosis codes§§\nRespiratory syndrome 2,355 117.8 740 148.0 30.3 <0.001\nAsthma 434 21.7 202 40.4 18.7 0.001\nBronchitis 247 12.4 82 16.4 4.1 0.3\nChest pain 904 45.2 223 44.6 -0.6 0.9\nCough 175 8.8 42 8.4 -0.4 0.9\nDyspnea 326 16.3 118 23.6 7.3 <0.001\n* Pre-fire period includes the 20 weekdays during September 24–October 19, 2007.\n† Fire period includes October 22–26, 2007.\n§ Mean number of visits during fire period minus mean number of visits during pre-fire period.\n¶ Kruskal-Wallis test.\n** Free-text chief complaints are parsed for specified keywords and assigned to syndromes and subsyndromes.\n†† Syndrome definitions were created by a multi-agency working group to assist in International Classification of Diseases, Ninth Revision, Clinical Modification\n(ICD-9-CM) code-based surveillance for bioterrorism-associated diseases (definitions available at http://www.bt.cdc.gov/surveillance/syndromedef/\nword/syndromedefinitions.doc). The respiratory syndrome includes codes for the following: acute infection of the upper and/or lower respiratory tract (from\nthe oropharynx to the lungs; includes otitis media); specific diagnosis of acute respiratory tract infection, such as pneumonia attributed to parainfluenza\nvirus; acute nonspecific diagnosis of respiratory tract infection, such as sinusitis, pharyngitis, and laryngitis; and acute nonspecific symptoms of respiratory tract\ninfection, such as cough, stridor, shortness of breath, and throat pain.\n§§ ICD-9-CM codes included in the respiratory syndrome available at http://www.bt.cdc.gov/surveillance/syndromedef/word/syndromedefinitions.doc. Other\ncodes are as follows: asthma, 493; bronchitis, 466 and 490; chest pain, 786.5; cough, 786.2; and dyspnea, 786.0.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":641,"renderedHeight":369,"naturalWidth":641,"naturalHeight":369,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 2275 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":74610},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/images/spacer.gif","alt":" ","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":10,"renderedHeight":1,"naturalWidth":10,"naturalHeight":10,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"DECORATIVE","altReason":"alt=\"\" (decorative)","bytes":821},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/headers_footers/images/spacer1.gif","alt":"","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":true,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":1,"renderedHeight":1,"naturalWidth":10,"naturalHeight":10,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"DECORATIVE","altReason":"alt=\"\" (decorative)","bytes":821},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/images/spacer1.gif","alt":"","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":true,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":1,"renderedHeight":1,"naturalWidth":10,"naturalHeight":10,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"DECORATIVE","altReason":"alt=\"\" (decorative)","bytes":821},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/images/s.gif","alt":"","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":true,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":20,"renderedHeight":1,"naturalWidth":1,"naturalHeight":1,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"DEC